{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 35,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.088,
            0.462,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Always True. We can write $n ^ { 4 }   = ( n ^ { 2 } ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.137,
            0.361,
            0.191
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Always True. $\\frac{n^{5}}{n^{3}} = n^{2}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.197,
            0.513,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": "(iv) Always True. $(n_{1})^{3} \\times (n_{2})^{3} = (n_{1} \\times n_{2})^{3} = (n_{1}n_{2})^{3}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.246,
            0.838,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": "(v) Never True. $q ^ { 4 6 } .$ , here q is prime number and 46 is not divisible by 4 and 6."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.296,
            0.652,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": "5. Simplify and write these in the exponential form. (i) $1 0 ^ { - 2 } \\times 1 0 ^ { - 5 }$ (ii) $5 ^ { 7 } \\div 5 ^ { 4 }$ (iii) $9 ^ { -   7 } \\div 9 ^ { 4 }$ (iv) $( 1 3 ^ { -   2 } ) ^ { - 3 }$ (v) $m ^ { 5 } n ^ { 1 2 } ( m n ) ^ { 9 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.359,
            0.333,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (i) $1 0 ^ { 7 }$ or $\\frac { 1 } { 1 0 ^ { 7 } }$ (ii) $5 ^ { 3 }$ (iii) $9 ^ { - 1 1 }$ or $\\frac { 1 } { 9 ^ { 1 1 } }$ (iv) $1 3 ^ { 6 }$ (v) $m ^ { 1 4 }   n ^ { 2 1 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.512,
            0.632,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": "6. If $1 2 ^ { 2 } = 1 4 4$ what is (i) $( 1 . 2 ) ^ { 2 }$ (ii) $(0.12)^{2}$ (iii) $( 0 . 0 1 2 ) ^ { 2 }$ (iv) $1 2 0 ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.575,
            0.416,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** If $(12)^{2} = 144,  then$ (i) $(1.2)^{2} = 1.44$ (ii) $(0.12)^{2} = 0.0144$ (iii) $(0.012)^{2} = 0.0001\\bar{4}4$ (iv) $(120)^{2} = 14400$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.678,
            0.762,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": "7. Circle the numbers that are the same— $2 ^ { 4 }   \\times   3 ^ { 6 }$ $6 ^ { 4 } \\times 3 ^ { 2 }$ $6 ^ { 1 0 }$ $1 8 ^ { 2 } \\times 6 ^ { 2 }$ $6 ^ { 2 4 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.726,
            0.543,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** $2^{4} \\times 3^{6}, 6^{4} \\times 3^{2}$ and $1 8 ^ { 2 } \\times 6 ^ { 2 }$ are same."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.756,
            0.788,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "8. Identify the greater number in each of the following— (i) $4^{3}    or   \\bar{3}^{4}$ (ii) $2 ^ { 8 }   \\mathrm { o r }   8 ^ { 2 }$ (iii) $1 0 0 ^ { 2 }$ or $2 ^ { 1 0 0 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.806,
            0.452,
            0.882
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (i) $3 ^ { 4 }$ is greater than $4 ^ { 3 }$ (ii) $2 ^ { 8 }$ is greater than $8 ^ { 2 }$ (iii) $2 ^ { 1 0 0 }$ is greater than $1 0 ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.859,
            0.92,
            0.878,
            0.94
          ],
          "content": "7"
        }
      ]
    }
